.TH LINDESK\-DATA 1 "2026" "lindesk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lindesk\-data \- maintain and query the lindesk telemetry lake
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lindesk\-data
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-backend
.BR auto | extension | native ]
.RB [ \-\-extension\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.I COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
lindesk records pressure, per-unit usage, events and metrics into a hive-partitioned
Vortex lake.
.B lindesk\-data
compacts sealed hour partitions, maintains the 1-minute and 1-hour rollups, applies
retention and regenerates
.IR catalog.duckdb ,
a views-only database that any DuckDB client can open read-only. It runs from
.I lindesk\-compact.timer
(system and user instances) and only touches partitions older than the current hour,
under the lake's lock. The same operations are available as
.B "lindeskctl data"
and
.BR "lindeskctl query" ,
which run this program.
.PP
.B lindesk\-data
and the lake writer (the
.B telemetry
plugin) ship in the optional
.B lindesk\-telemetry
package; the core
.B lindesk
package links neither DuckDB nor Vortex.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B maintain
Compact, prune and regenerate the catalog (what the timer runs).
.TP
.B compact
Merge each sealed hour's files and refresh the rollups.
.TP
.B prune
Apply retention:
.BR telemetry.retention.raw ,
.BR rollup_1m ,
.B rollup_1h
and
.BR max_size .
.TP
.B catalog
Regenerate
.IR catalog.duckdb .
Needs the DuckDB
.B vortex
extension; clients must run
.B "INSTALL vortex; LOAD vortex;"
before using its views (DuckDB does not autoload it).
.TP
.B install\-extension
Install the DuckDB
.B vortex
extension into the extension directory (needs network once), so queries and the catalog
work offline afterwards.
.TP
.B stats
Partitions, files, rows and bytes per table.
.TP
.BI query " SQL " "\fR[\fB\-\-format\fR table|csv|json|parquet] [\fB\-\-output\fR " FILE ]
Run one read-only statement.
.TP
.BI "delete \-\-where " PREDICATE " \fR[\fB\-\-table\fR " T "\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR " TIME "\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR " TIME "\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]"
Delete matching rows from raw tables and rollups. Without
.B \-\-yes
only counts them.
.TP
.B purge \-\-yes
Remove all telemetry.
.TP
.BI "export \-\-table " T " \fR[\fB\-\-from\fR " TIME "\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR " TIME "\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR jsonl|json]"
Print the rows of one table in a time window, with
.B ts
as epoch milliseconds (what
.B "lindeskctl simulate"
replays).
.TP
.BI import\-bench " RESULTS.json"
Store a
.B lindesk\-bench
results file in
.B bench_runs
and
.BR bench_samples .
.B lindesk\-bench run
does this itself when
.B lindesk\-data
is installed.
.TP
.B shell
Open the
.B duckdb
CLI read-only on the catalog (regenerating it if needed).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-root " DIR"
Lake root (also
.BR LINDESK_TELEMETRY_DIR ).
Default:
.B telemetry.dir
from the config, else
.I /var/lib/lindesk/telemetry
as root or
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/lindesk/telemetry
otherwise.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Config to read retention from (default
.I /etc/lindesk/lindesk.toml
as root, else the user's).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print reports as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-backend " auto|extension|native"
How
.I .vortex
files are read: the DuckDB
.B vortex
extension, the built-in Rust reader (offline; slower, memory-bound), or
.B auto
(the extension when it loads, else the built-in reader; the default).
.TP
.BI \-\-extension\-dir " DIR"
DuckDB extension directory (default
.IR <root>/../duckdb\-ext ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lindeskctl (1),
.BR lindeskd (8),
.BR lindesk\-session (1),
.BR duckdb (1)
